id: pm-y7s6
title: Type the flag tables and preset dispatch against real SDK contracts
description: "Annotate every flag table as FlagDefinition and migrate all 15 flag declarations from the deprecated type field to the canonical value_type, so the flag contract is enforced at compile time rather than resolved by the runtime fallback. Replace the last any-typed signature in the package, the preset dispatch table, with the real CommandHandlerContext."
type: Chore
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-26T19:03:06.099Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-26T19:03:07.207Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-26T19:03:07.206Z"
author: claude-orchestrator
acceptance_criteria: "All six flag tables annotated FlagDefinition; zero remaining deprecated type declarations; zero any in src; typecheck and full test suite green; flags verified to parse and behave correctly in a live pm host including boolean, string and dry-run combinations."
resolution: Flag tables typed as FlagDefinition and migrated to value_type; preset dispatch table typed with CommandHandlerContext. Package is now free of any.
expected_result: Flag contracts enforced at edit time; runtime behaviour unchanged.
actual_result: "46/46 tests green, typecheck clean. Verified in a live pm host: extension activates with activation_status ok and failed_count 0; 'presets list' and the boolean --json flag render correctly; 'presets apply kanban --dry-run' with and without the string flag --prefix, in both flag orders, left settings.json byte-identical and created no templates."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-26T19:03:06.838Z",claude-orchestrator,"FlagDefinition.type is deprecated in favour of value_type and only resolves via a runtime fallback (value_type ?? type). Untyped flag arrays hide that entirely, so the deprecation is invisible until the fallback is removed. Annotating the array is what surfaces it."
close_reason: completed
body: ""
